{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact 749ab713b8ba428a3a8c7504a1b9bf243c36d503, all fourteen artifacts, primary a63d91c4aee2a1912168cc39f7052a0f377a0926. This is the second review under #20424 / 1cb654fcee01c38a1f47996d82a2146de26e9e56, against the corrections to ratified verdict318bec67. The prior four Go counterexamples and two mounted DOM counterexamples now pass. The small-file out-of-range and unreturned-truncation findings are resolved. Two related boundary cases still fail, and the required history proof remains incomplete.\n\nSW-R2-01 (blocking; continuation of SW-01): backward-selected start is not an end bound for the next forward request. At internal/service/previewwindow.go@749ab713b8ba428a3a8c7504a1b9bf243c36d503:162, previousStart walks backwards to a byte-bounded start, but the later windowFor request runs forwardWindow from that start without the intended end. Reproduce content = strings.Repeat(strings.Repeat(\"w\",4000)+\"\\n\",19)+strings.Repeat(\"a\\n\",81); windowFor(content,20,0) returns current20–100, previous4. Following that Previous via windowFor(content,20,4) returns4–100, not a window ending19. The whole current window remains in the alleged previous window and Next is absent. This contradicts the API/window comment and reading-view.md's promise that Previous ends just before the current window. Uniform-width tests conceal it. Make both navigation directions use consistent verified-file partitions, or represent and enforce the intended endpoint. Test varying widths at cited-line fallback, explicit starts, next/back traversal and final windows, proving actual content/range/links agree.\n\nSW-R2-02 (continuation of SW-04): ui/src/components/Preview.tsx@749ab713b8ba428a3a8c7504a1b9bf243c36d503:123 treats every empty content string as an empty file/window. A real one-line blank partial window has empty content too. For a file of400 a-lines followed by one blank line, the producer legitimately answers content=\"\", window={start:401,end:401,total:401,partial:true}. The mounted real Preview renders zero rows under 'Lines401–401 of401', so a cited blank line cannot be displayed or highlighted. Derive row presence/count from the window metadata and the agreed trailing-newline convention, not string truthiness. Add the one-blank-line partial-window producer/consumer control and keep empty-file/out-of-range/trailing-newline cases green.\n\nSW-R2-03 (unresolved SW-05): ui/test/preview-window.test.mjs@749ab713b8ba428a3a8c7504a1b9bf243c36d503:106 now clicks Previous and round-trips its href through parseAddress. That is useful, but the harness still mounts Preview with a preconstructed target, never opens an actual review source link, never invokes the application's history handler or Back/Forward/reload, and assigns the final target directly. The comment 'so history holds it' and the request's full-browser-path claim remain unsupported. Exercise the existing routing consumer from an actual rendered review link, navigate middle/final and Previous, then reload or remount from the real address and run Back/Forward through the actual handler. Preserve exact revision and highlight. The relevant routing omissions must fail. Another serialization assertion does not satisfy the original condition.\n\nArchitecture: layers1 and7 retain the separate4 MiB verified-blob read and400-line/64 KiB/4 KiB-line response bounds, with same-head architecture and reading-view changes. All14 previews are ready and byte-exact; the reviewed embed reproduces. The navigation and source-row contract is still violated by SW-R2-01/02, and the claimed history behavior needs SW-R2-03 proof. Keep the final documented selection rule consistent with both producer and consumer.\n\nSecurity: inspected the correction and retained verified Git reads, exact event/head eligibility and attachment ownership, literal paths, same-origin bounded JSON, UTF-8/type refusals, deadline/cancellation/concurrency and inert React output. No new signing/fold/custody authority or independent trust bypass found. The failures are truthful selection/presentation and validation failures; preserve all existing security boundaries. This directly assigned implementation does not claim a new decision through an authority-bearing request chain.\n\nSimplification: a backward start guessed separately from a forward extent creates SW-R2-01. Use one coherent partition/range rule and one metadata-based line-count rule. Keep the existing dialog and routing surface. Production PreviewContentLimit remains used only as a historical test threshold; moving that fixture constant out of the production API is a minor cleanup, not the reason for this verdict.\n\nIndependent validation: locked npm ci --ignore-scripts, tsc/build and make ui-check reproduce the embed; UI222/222; go vet ./...; fresh service/gitstore TestPreview suites; fresh docset gates. Original six failure cases pass; the new production-window and mounted-DOM cases fail as described. Reproduction sources/logs retained at /tmp/git-window-r2-repro_test.go, /tmp/git-window-r2-repro.test.mjs, /tmp/git-window-r2-repros.log and /tmp/git-window-r2-ui-repros.log. Full Go and fourteen omission reruns are not claimed for this rejected head and remain required at the corrected review. Ratify this verdict, keep corrections on promise2cd413d6, publish the new exact head/current artifacts and request fresh independent review. No live reader replacement.\n","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a63d91c4aee2a1912168cc39f7052a0f377a0926","binding":"assigned","head":"749ab713b8ba428a3a8c7504a1b9bf243c36d503","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:954d8906a33e13111f4fa77f71f72c3b2205254a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2cd413d69d8a7111038fc086ee9f595d86a2662f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:954d8906a33e1